From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8550 mdp RCG ops

dispcc-sm8550.c -- "Fix disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src ops", retargeted from
dispcc-sm8450 (same node, same shape), from "SM8450 QoL changes (dispcc)"
(lore.kernel.org, Esteban Urrutia, Reviewed-by Konrad Dybcio).
clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops leaves the frequency alone at registration
instead of parking the RCG, which upstream wants because the park shows as a
flicker on a bootloader-lit panel -- ours.

This patch used to carry the Lucid Ole PLL guard too. 7.3.6 has that guard as
ff94db2cd6c9 ("clk: qcom: alpha-pll: Check Lucid Ole PLL status before
configuring"), and the pinned tree must keep it: without it this hunk is FATAL,
in a way nothing reports. Measured on an AYANEO Pocket ACE, before the guard:

  this hunk alone, no flag   -> BLACK PANEL   (build 20260907T094603Z)
  this hunk alone, with flag -> BLACK PANEL   (build 20260907T100424Z)
  guard alone                -> works, warning 0 (build 20260907T120035Z)
  both                       -> works, warning 0 (build 20260907T122602Z)

Without the .init park the RCG stays sourced from whatever the bootloader left
running, and without the guard probe then reprograms exactly that PLL underneath
it. The black builds reported no warning, no underrun, no vblank timeout,
backlight on, connector connected, gamescope presenting and flips completing.
Only a human looking at the panel could tell them from a good build.

This also drops a LOCAL GUESS that lived here: CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE, whose
commit message claimed it fixed the "rcg didn't update its configuration"
warning. It never did -- the flag covers .set_rate and .set_parent while the
failing update comes from .init. The node is byte-for-byte the upstream shape,
matching dispcc-x1e80100.

COVERS BOTH SHIPPING SoCs: dispcc-sm8550.c serves SM8650 too, via
`{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-dispcc" }` in its match table.

The sm8450 halves are upstream; this sm8550 retarget is not, and should be sent.

Signed-off-by: Esteban Urrutia <esteuwu@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8550.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8550.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8550.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8550.c
@@ -622,7 +622,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src = {
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_8,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_8),
 		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops,
 	},
 };
